|******************************************************************************
| A made-up device for the example `examples/ibis_signal_integrity`: a 3.3 V
| LVCMOS output and input, and an LVDS-like differential output and input with
| an on-die 100 ohm termination. The values do not describe a real device:
| the tables follow simple formulas (a driver saturating like a transistor,
| clamp diodes with 2 ohms in series), not measurements. The edges are given by
| [Ramp] only; files from vendors usually have [Rising Waveform] and
| [Falling Waveform] tables as well, which cuprite_wire uses when present.
|******************************************************************************
[IBIS Ver]      5.0
[File Name]     demo_io.ibs
[File Rev]      1.0
[Date]          2026-11-23
[Source]        Written by hand for the examples of cuprite_wire.
[Disclaimer]    Not a real device.

[Component]     DEMO-IO
[Manufacturer]  None (a made-up device)
[Package]
| variable  typ       min       max
R_pkg       0.2       0.15      0.3
L_pkg       2.5nH     2.0nH     3.0nH
C_pkg       0.6pF     0.5pF     0.7pF
[Pin]  signal_name  model_name
1      CLK_OUT      LVCMOS33_OUT
2      CLK_IN       LVCMOS33_IN
3      TX_P         LVDS_OUT
4      TX_N         LVDS_OUT
5      RX_P         LVDS_IN
6      RX_N         LVDS_IN
7      VDD33        POWER
8      VDD25        POWER
9      GND          GND
[Diff Pin]  inv_pin  vdiff  tdelay_typ  tdelay_min  tdelay_max
3           4        NA     0ns         NA          NA
5           6        100mV  NA          NA          NA
| The receiver's termination between its pins.
[Series Pin Mapping]  pin_2  model_name
5                     6      ODT100

